WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.104
Step 1. Open the schedule.

1.2
00:00:02.104 --> 00:00:06.738
An exception marks a period when a practitioner is not available,

1.3
00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:09.305
across all their schedule templates.

1.4
00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:14.440
Open the account menu, select Profile, then the Availability tab.

2.1
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.143
Step 2. Open the exception form.

2.2
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:21.206
Select the Exceptions tab, then select Add Exception.

2.3
00:00:21.206 --> 00:00:24.772
The Add Schedule Exceptions sheet opens.

3.1
00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:26.966
Step 3. Enter the reason.

3.2
00:00:26.966 --> 00:00:32.252
In Reason, enter why you are not available, here Department meeting.

3.3
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:34.850
The form requires a reason.

4.1
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.936
Step 4. Set the period.

4.2
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:43.561
In Valid Period, select the Start date and the End date, here 28 November for both,

4.3
00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:48.531
then select Apply. You cannot select a day before today.

5.1
00:00:48.531 --> 00:00:50.625
Step 5. Set the times.

5.2
00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:56.663
Enter the start time in From and the end time in To, here 11 AM to 1 PM.

5.3
00:00:56.663 --> 00:01:02.948
If the exception starts today, the start time must be later than now.

6.1
00:01:02.948 --> 00:01:08.159
Step 6. Confirm the unavailability. Select Confirm Unavailability.

6.2
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:14.397
Care shows Exception created successfully and lists the exception on the Exceptions

6.3
00:01:14.397 --> 00:01:19.558
tab. Care refuses it if a booked slot starts within its times.
